{
  "slug": "prompt-squeeze",
  "name": "Prompt Squeeze",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "prompt-squeeze builds prompt-cost discipline into Claude Code via three surfaces:\n\n/squeeze skill that compresses a verbose prompt into a token-efficient equivalent and renders a side-by-side markdown comparison plus a cited receipt (dollars saved, Wh saved, CO₂e at US-grid average).\n\nUserPromptSubmit hook that meters every prompt, nudges Claude when ≥25% compressible, and (in interactive mode) blocks prompts above a configurable token limit while showing a 2-column ASCII diff so the user can review before sending.\n\nAn MCP server exposing personal_stats, team_stats, and weekly_report tools that aggregate the local hook log into shareable rollups.",
  "longDescription": "Ships **1 skill**, **4 commands**, **1 hook** and **1 MCP server**.\n\n- **Skills** (1): `prompt-squeeze` (Rewrite the user's draft prompt into a token-efficient equivalent and report dollar + electricity savings)\n- **Commands** (4): `sq` (Resume a pending squeeze (y/n) or manage session consent (undo/off)), `squeeze-config` (Walk through prompt-squeeze settings), `squeeze-stats` (Show personal prompt-squeeze savings (last 7 days)), `squeeze` (Compress a prompt and show savings)\n- **Hooks** (1): `UserPromptSubmit`\n- **MCP servers** (1): `prompt-squeeze-stats`\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install prompt-squeeze@claude-community` from `joshua-burnell-1/prompt-squeeze`.",
  "compatibility": [
    "claude"
  ],
  "pluginType": "package",
  "package": {
    "skill": 1,
    "hook": 1,
    "command": 4,
    "mcp": 1
  },
